---
id: org.dxos.spec.fixture
name: Fixture
version: 0.1.0
extends:
  - org.dxos.spec.core
---

Cases the real specs do not all exercise. Prose outside a fence stays markdown: [F-1] is a link
reference here, not an MDL cross-reference.

```mdl
diagram-rule DR-1: An unknown, hyphenated block type is still a type
  severity: warn | error   # a union with a trailing comment
  tags: [smoke, nightly]
  covers: []
```

```mdl
type Piece
  # a whole-line comment
  kind: PieceKind
  color?: Color
  moves: Move[]
  ref: Ref<Board>
  active: true
  weight: 1..10
  label?: "pawn" | "rook"
```

```mdl
feat F-1: Refers to [F-1.2] and [op:Move] in its title
  Inline prose before the first field, with `code`, "a string" and $given.space.
  req F-1.1: White moves first; see type:Board and op:Move.
  req F-1.2: The rule in org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0 applies. A # in a sentence is a comment.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Two deciders stay two entries. Fills in [D-1, D-2].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:alice
  affects: [Scene, F-2.1]
  desc: |
    A block scalar: key: value lines in here are prose, not fields,
    and user:bob is still an actor.
  rejected:
    - One entry with both deciders: hides who chose what.
```

~~~mdl
op Move
  key: org.dxos.operation.chess.move
~~~
